{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Moses went out.</b> He did not refrain, despite his eminence, from going forth to greet one who had done him kindness in time of distress — as in וְאֶת מַאֲמַר מָרְדֳּכַי אֶסְתֵּר עֹשָׂה כוּ' (Esther 2:20), and as in Joseph's conduct toward his brothers when he was king. The opposite is וְלֹא זָכַר שַׂר הַמַּשְׁקִים אֶת יוֹסֵף (Genesis 40:23)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:03.420596102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}